{#
  PersistentVolumeClaim for a k8s-hosted service — the plain RWO/longhorn-family body that
  authelia, crowdsec, loki-homelab, mosquitto, pihole (both claims), registry, valheim-stats and
  wg-easy share. Each carries its own WHY for the storage class / backup posture it picked,
  which stays at the call site (via `{% call %}`) rather than being swallowed here — the whole
  point of these comments is that they differ role to role.

  THE CALLER SLOT SITS BETWEEN `spec:` AND `accessModes:`, so a comment that governs
  `storageClassName` cannot sit on that line here. A `k8s_claims` role keeps that kind of
  reasoning beside its `*_storage_class` default instead, which is the line that makes the
  trade-off there: valheim's nobackup install claim and pi-peer-backup's "Plain `longhorn` ON
  PURPOSE (not -nobackup)" both do this.

  `claim-default.yaml.j2` calls this macro once per entry of a role's `k8s_claims`, which is
  how the roles converted under #3387 create their claims. `_rendered_pvc_claims` reads
  `k8s_claims` from the role's defaults, so a claim declared there stays visible to
  test_k8s_autodeploy_guard.py::test_snapshot_pvc_declarations_match_rendered_claims. A role
  template that calls this macro does not: that reader greps a template's text for a literal
  `kind: PersistentVolumeClaim` block and renders no Jinja. See "Textual guard checks break on
  an indirection" in project memory.

  Arguments:
    name           PVC name; matches whatever claimName a Deployment mounts.
    storage_class  e.g. `longhorn`, `longhorn-nobackup`, or a role's own `*_k8s_storage_class`.
    size           e.g. a role's own `*_k8s_storage` / `*_k8s_size` default.
    namespace      defaults to the shared `k8s_namespace`, same idiom as ingressroute.yml.j2's
                   `namespace | default(k8s_namespace, true)`. observability's four claims (loki,
                   prometheus, grafana, tempo) pass `k8s_observability_namespace` through their
                   `k8s_claims` entries.
    access_modes   defaults to `['ReadWriteOnce']`. media-volume's `media-data` passes
                   `['ReadWriteMany']` through its `k8s_claims` entry; a claim's access modes are
                   immutable once created, so this must match the live claim.

  Call with a body to insert a comment block between `spec:` and `accessModes:`; call plain
  (no `{% call %}`) when there's nothing to say there.
#}
{% macro pvc(name, storage_class, size, namespace=none, access_modes=none) -%}
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: {{ name }}
  namespace: {{ namespace | default(k8s_namespace, true) }}
spec:
{% if caller is defined %}{{ caller() }}{% endif %}
  accessModes:
    - {{ (access_modes or ['ReadWriteOnce']) | join('\n    - ') }}
  storageClassName: {{ storage_class }}
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: {{ size }}
{% endmacro %}
